  "task": "missing-duplicate-string",
  "experiment": "corrected-dataset-fix (MDF1: dataset construction + audit)",
  "description": "Corrected missing-duplicate-string dataset preserving Butoi et al.'s mixed negative-generation strategy (50% uniform-random / 50% adversarial) but replacing the K-edit-perturbation adversarial half with an explicit hard-negative construction: a genuine positive (w+w with one '1' blanked), with two adjacent DIFFERING positions swapped within the half not containing the blank -- preserving blank count, sequence length, and that half's content multiset (hence per-half aggregate counts stay matched), breaking only the true position-by-position duplicate check. Framing and shortcut-feature list corrected against phase3_missdup_task_audit.json (see module docstring) -- the blank is a constant '1' redaction, not a 'which symbol' identification target, and the four REAL shortcut features (not the six stack-manipulation ones the request named) are verified against every hard negative.",
