  "known_simplifications_vs_original_pipeline": [
    "No cross-split deduplication of positive examples (negligible given the string space size at these lengths, matching every prior fix experiment's own documented simplification).",
    "Hard-negative construction rejects (resamples the base positive entirely) when half < 2 or the swap-eligible half is monochromatic -- a minor, documented distributional deviation for the hard-negative half only.",
    "supports_log_probability() is False for this task (confirmed in source) -- no log-probabilities.txt is written, matching the original languages/missing-duplicate-string dataset's own file set.",
